  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Multiprofile + avgpool is the strongest evidence so far, with rna_only scgpt avgpool best (acc 0.5305, F1 0.5152) and multimodal scgpt/vit_l avgpool concat close but lower. The main untested uncertainty is whether this result depends specifically on scgpt or on multiprofile RNA representation generally. config_015 keeps the promising multiprofile/avgpool/RNA-only setting and changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200, isolating the representation effect. This is a better use of budget than another multimodal tweak because multimodal has not yet beaten the simpler RNA-only model, and clarifying RNA encoder importance may guide both high-accuracy selection and model simplification."
}

